"""AMRAL NS symbol table ingestion into a local SEDB database.

Scope (updated 2026-08-25, built by 見證):
  - Framework-level notation shared across the whole PROGRAM-NS corpus
    (C1/C2/C3/C4/C5/C6).
  - Full symbol-level detail for the entire C6 sub-series, C6-A through
    C6-Q (backfilled 2026-08-24).
  - Full symbol-level detail for C1, C2, the entire C3 sub-series (C3-A
    through C3-Y, 25 rounds), the entire C4 sub-series (C4-A through C4-J,
    9 rounds, no C4-H), and the entire C5 sub-series (C5-A through C5-M,
    13 rounds) -- backfilled 2026-08-25, 1485 entries read verbatim from
    source .md files via parallel extraction agents (Claude subagents for
    C1-C3 and part of C4; Grok 4.6 / Gemini 3.1 Pro via Vertex AI for the
    remainder of C4 and all of C5). Cross-round symbol recurrence (e.g.
    Q_SV, lambda_2^+, enstrophy E_R) is largely self-documented in each
    entry's own "notes" field, quoting the source round's own citation of
    where the symbol was first introduced, rather than hand-curated here.

NOT yet covered (flagged honestly, not silently skipped):
  - BSD, Moser, skew-field, P/NP-dual, GLC, CPL, CCM, Riemann series.

Re-run is idempotent: entity ids are deterministic, and set_cell()
overwrites existing cells rather than duplicating them. Extending this
script (new series, new rounds) means appending to SYMBOLS below and
re-running.
"""

